- US-2-AC3: met — Single <input type="file" multiple> feeding one form; the change handler iterates fileInput.files and renders the whole set as one list with an empty state, and the confirmation reports the packet count from the same input. Documents stay associated with the one submission for the scope of this page.
- US-2-AC4: NOT MET — No policy enforcement exists at all. The file input declares no accept filter; the change handler only formats names and sizes — there is no type check, no size check, no rejection, and no message. The developer's own test_upload_policy_enforcement_is_absent explicitly pins the absence rather than testing the criterion, so the 7 passing tests include one that asserts this criterion is unimplemented. 'No partial file is retained' is only vacuously true because nothing is ever stored.
- US-2-AC6: met — On submit the handler preventDefaults, hides the form and reveals the confirmation panel immediately with a generated reference (MS-YYYY-MM-NNNN), a Received status pill, member, timestamp, document count and first day absent, plus instruction to quote the reference. Displayed synchronously, no network. See notes on reference uniqueness.
- US-2-AC5: NOT MET — Not in the criteria list supplied to this review and not assessed. Flagged only so the gap in the id sequence (AC1–AC4, AC6) is visible in the run record rather than read as complete coverage.

Reviewer notes: ['Verdict is fail: US-2-AC2 and US-2-AC4 are unmet. Two of the five criteria reviewed are not satisfied, and neither is a cosmetic gap — one is the governance step (attestation), the other is the input-validation policy.', 'The passing pytest run is not evidence of acceptance. Six of the seven tests assert that markup elements exist, not that behaviour occurs; the seventh asserts an acceptance criterion is NOT implemented. A green suite here is compatible with an unmet criterion, which is exactly why the criteria were checked against the source rather than the test result.', 'Credit where due: the developer did not fake AC4. test_upload_policy_enforcement_is_absent records the gap in the open, with a note to flip it when the check lands. That is the right behaviour under the staged-output discipline and should not be penalised — but it does not convert an unmet criterion into a met one.', "Fabrication risk, and the most serious finding outside the criteria: the member lookup falls back to a hard-coded 'Alex Moreau' record for ANY unrecognised policy/member combination. A typo produces a confidently rendered, entirely invented member — name, DOB, earnings, coverage — that the sponsor is then asked to attest is accurate. A lookup that cannot fail cannot identify. It should return a not-found state, and the fallback record should be removed before this is shown to anyone.", "The reference number is Math.random() over a 4-digit space with no persistence or collision check, so two submissions in the same month collide roughly 1 in 9000. Acceptable for a demo, not for the 'unambiguous' wording of AC6; worth a note wherever the reference is described.", "The page carries a 'Demo data' badge in the sub-heading, but the confirmation panel — the artifact a viewer is most likely to screenshot — carries no staged marking, and its copy ('Intake has received the documents', 'the status will update in SponsorConnect') asserts backend behaviour that does not exist. 